# Express API

## Module structure

Feature modules under `src/modules/`:

```
src/modules/org/
├── org.routes.ts
├── org.controller.ts
├── org.service.ts
└── org.schema.ts
```

Mount routers from `src/routes/index.ts`.

## Request flow

```text
Request → validate(Zod) → requireSession → requireActiveOrg → requireOrgPermission → controller → service → Prisma
```

## Controllers

- Thin — parse params, call service, return JSON envelope
- Use `asyncHandler` — never bare async functions in routes
- Never access Prisma directly from controllers

## Services

- Business logic + `assertOrgMember()` + `requireOrgPermission()`
- Throw `ForbiddenError` / `NotFoundError` from `tenant-guard.ts`
- All org-scoped queries include `where: { organizationId }`

## Validation

- Zod schemas in `*.schema.ts` per module
- `validate({ body, query, params })` middleware
- OpenAPI via `@asteasolutions/zod-to-openapi`: register paths in `src/api-docs/openapi.ts` with `registry.registerPath()` (not auto-synced from route files; no decorators)
- When adding a v1 endpoint, add a matching `registerPath` entry — route Zod schemas in `*.routes.ts` are separate unless you extract and reuse them

## Response envelope

Success:

```json
{ "success": true, "data": {}, "meta": { "requestId": "..." } }
```

Error:

```json
{ "success": false, "error": { "code": "...", "message": "..." }, "meta": { "requestId": "..." } }
```

Paginated lists include `page`, `limit`, `totalResults`, `totalPages` in `data`.

## Versioning

- All business endpoints under `/api/v1/*`
- Auth endpoints at `/api/auth/*` (Better Auth — not versioned)
- OpenAPI UI at `GET /api/v1/docs`

